1. **Data Collection**: Collect data on inventory levels, customer purchases, and preferences. You can use JavaScript to fetch this data from your backend database or API.

2. **Alert System**: To alert the inventory manager when an item is consistently going out of stock, you can use JavaScript to monitor inventory levels and send notifications when a threshold is reached. For example, you can set a threshold of 5 units and send a notification when the inventory level drops below that.

3. **Personalized Notifications**: To personalize notifications for back-in-stock items, you can use JavaScript to store customer preferences in a cookie or local storage. When an item is back in stock, you can check these preferences and send a notification only to customers who have expressed interest in that item.

