```

Here's a simple LDPC encoder in SystemVerilog for an FPGA implementation:

```verilog
module ldpc_encoder(
    input wire clk,
    input wire reset,
    input wire data_in,
    output wire data_out,
    parameter integer WIDTH = 8,
    parameter integer NUM_PARITY = 4
);

reg [WIDTH-1:0] data_reg;
reg [NUM_PARITY-1:0] parity_reg;

always @(posedge clk or posedge reset)
begin
    if (reset)
    begin
        data_reg <= 0;
        parity_reg <= 0;
    end
    else
    begin
        data_reg <= data_in;
        parity_reg <= ~data_reg & (2^NUM_PARITY-1);
    end
end

assign data_out = data_reg | parity_reg;

endmodule
```

This module takes a data input and generates a data output with added parity bits. The number of parity bits can be configured through the `NUM_PARITY` parameter.

