```
2. Create an instance of the AEAD GCM cipher class:
```java
Aead aead = Aead.newInstance("AES/GCM/NoPadding");
```
3. Generate a secret key and initialize the cipher:
```java
byte[] secretKey = AeadUtils.generateRandomBytes(32);
SecretKeySpec secretKeySpec = new SecretKeySpec(secretKey, "AES");
aead.init(Cipher.ENCRYPT_MODE, secretKeySpec);
```
4. Update the Authenticated Data (AAD) using the `updateAAD` method:
```java
byte[] aad = "your-authenticated-data".getBytes();
aead.updateAAD(aad);
```
5. Encrypt or decrypt data using the cipher:
```java
byte[] plaintext = "your-plaintext".getBytes();
byte[] ciphertext = aead.doFinal(plaintext);
// or
byte[] plaintext = aead.doFinal(ciphertext);
```
6. Close the cipher when you're done:
```java
aead.close();
```

