To set up Auth0 SSO (Single Sign-On) for multiple React apps, follow these steps:

1. Sign up for an Auth0 account and create a new application.
2. In the Auth0 dashboard, go to the "Applications" tab and select your newly created application.
3. Click on the "Settings" tab and scroll down to the "SSO" section.
4. Enable SSO and choose the "OpenID Connect" protocol.
5. Copy the "Issuer URL" and "Client ID" from the Auth0 dashboard.
6. In each of your React apps, install the `@auth0/auth0-react` package using npm or yarn.
7. Create a new file called `auth0-config.js` in each app and add the following code:
```javascript
import auth0 from '@auth0/auth0-react';

const auth0Config = {
  domain: 'your-domain.com', // Replace with your Auth0 domain
  clientId: 'your-client-id', // Replace with the Client ID copied from the Auth0 dashboard
  redirectUri: 'http://localhost:3000/callback', // Replace with the callback URL for your app
};

export default auth0Config;
```
Replace `your-domain.com` with your Auth0 domain and `your-client-id` with the Client ID copied from the Auth0 dashboard.

8. In each app, import the `auth0Config` object and use it to configure Auth0 in your components. For example:
```javascript
import React from 'react';
import { Auth0Provider } from '@auth0/auth0-react';
import auth0Config from './auth0-config';

function App() {
  return (
    <Auth0Provider
      domain={auth0Config.domain}
      clientId={auth0Config.clientId}
      redirectUri={auth0Config.redirectUri}
    >
      {/* Your app content goes here */}
    </Auth0Provider>
  );
}

export default App;
```
9. Finally, make sure to handle the authentication callback in each app. You can do this by adding a route for the `/callback` path and handling the

